8810 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This report covers the security review of the Ana\056fi source code\054 including the backend services\054 the execution engine\054 and the on\055chain wallet\054 paymaster\054 and delegation contracts\056\nDuring our review\054 we identified 1 high severity vulnerability\054 related to unbounded call tree depth in block traces\054 which could have allowed a single unprivileged transaction to permanently halt the engine\220s fold for every tenant\056\nAdditionally\054 we identified 4 medium severity vulnerabilities\056 Two of them stemmed from the backend not verifying the ERC\0551967 implementation slot of sponsored wallets\054 which could have allowed a wallet owner to upgrade to a malicious implementation and drain the paymaster\056 The other two related to missing bounds on client\055controlled gas fields\054 which could have inflated paymaster reimbursements\054 and on delegation caveat arrays\054 which could have been used to drain the executor EOA\056\nWe also identified 1 low severity vulnerability\054 which allowed the one\055active\055grant\055per\055wallet invariant to be bypassed in the activateGrant function\056\nAll of our reported issues were fixed by the development team and consequently validated by us\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 8811 0 R
     /Pg 728 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

